cau (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release v0.3.0.
  * The kernel guard's events say which process they happened to: the sensor
    records the process's start time in the same clock and unit as field 22 of
    /proc/<pid>/stat, so the engine can attribute an event to that process
    and to no other.
  * The host-behaviour inventories (an auditor library, a fanotify listener, a
    systemd generator, a pinned BPF object) no longer report the host's own
    systemd, and a package database that cannot answer is a note rather than a
    finding.
  * The model registry is a signed catalogue of the artifacts the engine may
    run, each with an SBOM and a model card.
  * The inference sidecar: the engine never loads a model into its own
    process; it asks a sidecar over a unix socket and gets scores back.
  * Firmware images are scanned as containers (squashfs, cramfs, ext, FAT,
    tar, zip, xz, zstd, uImage, ISO), not as one blob.
  * An evasion report measures how fragile each shipped detector is, and a
    temporal gate asks whether the content still catches what it caught in an
    earlier period of the corpus.
  * The pipeline runs on current runners and current actions, with an
    automated security lane (govulncheck, CodeQL, dependency review) and a
    release pipeline that publishes a main release, a patch release and a beta
    from one path.

 -- Stephan Botes <stephanbotes0@gmail.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:01:28 +0200

cau (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release v0.2.0.
  * Network plane: NDR with cross-domain correlation and blocking (cau net, cau defend --netblock).
  * Detection content updates: tradecraft extended with LOLBAS, GTFOBins, LOLC2/LOLFSaaS/LOTTunnels/LOTWebhooks catalogues.
  * Signed releases with integrity baseline and self-verifying binary.
  * Arch Linux packaging with native ARM64 builds.
  * Resident daemon (cau defend) with layered correlation, automatic response, and SIEM forwarding.
  * Performance improvements: prefilter reduces scan time, memory usage optimizations.

 -- Stephan Botes <stephanbotes0@gmail.com>  Sat, 08 Nov 2026 21:08:00 +0200

cau (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian and Kali Linux packaging.
  * Engine: one-read detection pipeline across hash signatures, YARA, string
    and API heuristics, static structure (entropy, packer, section and
    entry-point anomalies, TLSH/ssdeep/imphash similarity) and invisible-
    codepoint steganography, fused so sub-threshold sources that corroborate
    each other are reported SUSPICIOUS with the agreeing sources named.
  * Detections ignore code-signing certificates; verdicts carry a labeled
    class and a MITRE ATT&CK technique.
  * Machine-readable output with CI exit codes: text, JSON, SARIF and OCSF.
  * cau-mcp: the same engine served over the Model Context Protocol.
  * Bundled content: YARA rules, hash signatures, fuzzy-hash database, with
    an ATT&CK coverage gate in CI against a recorded technique list.
  * Optional systemd units (cau-daemon.service, cau-scan.service and
    cau-scan.timer) are installed but not enabled.
  * Signed releases: Ed25519-signed signature bundles and a self-verifying
    binary (cau verify-self).

 -- Stephan Botes <stephanbotes0@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:42:00 +0200
